.TH COF-MAN 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-man \- Show a cof man page through man, or print its roff when piped or
given --roff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof man [OPTIONS] [command]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a cof man page through man on a terminal, or prints its roff when piped
or given --roff. Works even where MANPATH doesn't reach the installed pages:
the pages are generated from the same code this command itself runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B COMMAND
Command to show the page for (default: cof itself).
.TP
.B --roff
Print the page's roff instead of showing it through man.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof man run
Shows cof-run(1) through man.
.TP
.B cof man run --roff | groff -man -Tutf8
Renders cof-run(1)'s roff directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The page was shown or printed.
.TP
.B 2
COMMAND doesn't name a page; the available pages are listed.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR
